Z||000000||Elliottnap||06-07-2000||09:20 PM||||I dunno if this is a dumb question...but was power steering available on fieros??  I have an 86 SE which has power everything but not steering!  Is it available and was it an option...if not, why??||||reg||1
Z||000001||sdm1964||06-07-2000||10:08 PM||||No Power steering was not offered on fieros,nor was it an option. The powers that be in detroit just didn't do it for some strange reason. I kinda like not having it. I did see a kit offered on the internet. You have to change out the rack, etc.||||reg||7
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||06-07-2000||11:59 PM||||I was thinking about getting a power steering kit, until I finally drove a GT... when I went back to driving my parents car.... I almost crashed it because the steering was so sloppy compared to the Fiero. hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>power steering is nice for parking maneuvers.... but I don't like it for driving anymore.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||06-08-2000||08:19 PM||||Elliot...<P>This has been discussed before.<P>Use the SEARCH function and use POWER STEERING as your keywords.||||reg||10
Z||000004||terryk||06-08-2000||11:49 PM||||Power steering was developed by not released to production. I guess a few executive cars had it installed.<P>I don't care what anyone says, power steering on a Fiero would be nice. A nice 2.75 ratio rack from an A car. I've seriously thought about it. Yep, it will steal some power.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Mattsfiero||06-09-2000||04:39 AM||||Wait power sterring in a sports car like the Fiero....I think not. The handling you get with manual steering is tighter then that of a power steering car. It allows you to feel the curves.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000006||Standard||06-09-2000||04:55 AM||||I hate power steering!  Makes me feel so.. disconnected from the road.  Power steering and sports cars just don't go together.. imnsho||||reg||1
Z||000007||jlruiz67||06-17-2000||10:05 PM||||Hello all<BR> I ran into this website, it has information on the Fiero Power Steering. I don't think you can buy the parts and build it but I hope one of you can prove me wrong and share information...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/MI_Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/MI_Fiero.htm</A> <P><BR>1988 Fiero Power Steering Pump/ Electro-Hydraulic<P><BR>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------<P><BR>1. RESERVOIR, Elec Hyd Pwr Strg Pump <BR>2. CAP, Reservoir <BR>3. WASHER, Flat (6mm Regular) <BR>4. NUT, Metric Hex Flange <BR>5. WASHER, Retaining <BR>6. BOLT, Hanger Mounting (M6x1) <BR>7. HANGER, Ehps Brkt <BR>8. SCREW, Hex Hd Tap (M5x0.8) <BR>9. BRACKET, Elec Hyd Pwr Strg <BR>10. PUMP, W/Mtr <BR>11. CLAMP, Reservoir Hose <BR>12. WASHER, Flat (6MM Regular) <BR>13. SCREW, Hex Washer Hd <BR>14. SCREW, Hex Hd Tap (M6x1) <BR>15. CONTROLLER, Elec hyd <BR>16. HOSE, Reservoir <P><BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<P>Description QTY Part Number <BR>PUMP, P.S. (PROD.) 1 7849457 <BR>PUMP KIT, W/EHPS MTR (SERVICE) 1 26003096 <BR>BOLT, HANGER MTG (M6X1) 2 26000620 <BR>BRACKET, E/H PWR STRG 1 26000628 <BR>CAP, RESERVOIR 1 26008138 <BR>CLAMP, RESERVOIR HOSE 2 26000890 <BR>CONTROLLER KIT, EHPS 1 22068247 <BR>HANGER KIT, EHPS BRKT 1 26007592 <BR>HOSE KIT, RESERVOIR 1 26007593 <BR>NUT, METRIC HEX FLANGE 2 26000849 <BR>RESERVOIR, E/H PWR STRG PUMP 1 26000889 <BR>SCREW, HEX HD TAP (M5X0.8) 4 26000614 <BR>SCREW, HEX HD TAP (M6X1) 2 26000613 <BR>WASHER, FLAT (6MM REGULAR) 2 26008220 <BR>WASHER, RETAINING 2 26000434 <P><BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<P>Return to the Michigan Fiero Page<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||contra||06-18-2000||07:01 PM||||The best option would be (and i think somebody else posted this a looong time ago, so i dont want to take credit, but it was a nice option) the same steering as the acura nsx's have in them. They've got power assist steering which works as power steering until you reach 10mph or so, then it shuts off and you become manual again.<BR>but...<BR>that'll probably never happen on a fiero i will own =/||||reg||10
Z||000009||Old Lar||06-18-2000||08:03 PM||||I've seen a couple of cars with a Mercury Mercur(sp?) power steering assist on a Fiero.  It worked as far as the owner told me, but he purchased the car that way.  The power steering unit was in the engine compartment with some long hydralic lines to the steering box.||||reg||4
